Policyholder Insurance Coverage and Services

Our comprehensive insurance policy includes:
- Auto insurance with liability coverage starting at $25,000
- Home insurance with dwelling coverage up to $500,000
- Life insurance with death benefit options from $100,000 to $2,000,000
- Health insurance with various deductible options
- Business liability coverage with customizable limits
- Umbrella policy options for additional protection
- Roadside assistance and towing services
- Claims processing with 24/7 support

Policy features include:
- Flexible payment plans (monthly, quarterly, annual)
- Multi-policy discounts up to 25%
- Safe driver rewards and accident forgiveness
- Online policy management and claims filing
- Mobile app for policy access and claims

To file a claim:
1. Contact claims department immediately
2. Provide policy number and incident details
3. Submit required documentation
4. Work with assigned claims adjuster
5. Receive settlement or repair authorization

Customer support available 24/7 at 1-800-POLICY-HELP

Policy Renewal Process:
- Automatic renewal 30 days before expiration
- Premium adjustments based on claims history
- Coverage modifications available during renewal
- Early renewal discounts for proactive customers

Address Change Process:
- Update address within 30 days of change
- Submit proof of new residence
- Update vehicle registration if applicable
- Premium adjustments for location changes

Payment Options and Premiums:
- Monthly automatic bank draft: Standard payment method
- Quarterly payments: 2% discount applied to total premium
- Annual payments: 5% discount applied to total premium
- Credit card payments: Accepted with 2.5% processing fee
- Online payment portal: Available 24/7 with instant confirmation
- Paper check payments: Processed within 3-5 business days
- Auto-pay enrollment: 1% additional discount for automatic payments
- Payment grace period: 15 days after due date before late fees
- Late payment fees: $25 for payments received after grace period
- Payment plan options: Available for customers experiencing financial hardship

Claims Reporting Timeline and Procedures:
- Auto accidents: Report within 24 hours for immediate assistance
- Property damage: Report within 48 hours for property claims
- Theft: Report immediately to police and insurer within 12 hours
- Medical claims: Submit within 30 days of service for timely processing
- Fire damage: Report within 4 hours for emergency response
- Natural disasters: Report within 72 hours for disaster claims
- Late reporting consequences: May affect coverage eligibility and claim processing
- Emergency claims: 24/7 hotline available for urgent situations
- Claims documentation: Submit within 14 days of initial report
- Claims status updates: Available online or by phone within 24 hours

Coverage Limits and Deductibles:
- Standard deductible: $500 for comprehensive, $1000 for collision
- Optional lower deductibles available at higher premium
- Maximum coverage limits vary by policy type
- Additional riders available for enhanced protection

Policy Modifications:
- Add/remove drivers: Processed within 24 hours
- Coverage adjustments: Effective next business day
- Vehicle additions: Immediate coverage upon verification
- Policy cancellations: 30-day notice required

Claims Processing Details:
- Initial response time: Within 4 hours for emergency claims
- Claims adjuster assignment: Within 24 hours of report
- Documentation review: 3-5 business days for standard claims
- Settlement timeline: 10-15 business days for approved claims
- Appeal process: Available for denied claims within 30 days
- Claims tracking: Real-time updates available online and mobile app
